From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: compiled resources, styles and templates (XBF dictionary, setter and template sections)

Programs ship their App.xaml, resource dictionaries and control templates compiled, and our compiled-XAML reader skipped those parts. It now reads a resource dictionary's section (keyed resources, implicit styles), a style's setters (by name or property ID, inline values, objects of the section, {StaticResource}/{ThemeResource} values), a style's TargetType, {StaticResource}/{ThemeResource} on members and as objects, and a ControlTemplate's content section, which is kept with the file and made again for each control it is applied to, its {TemplateBinding} members following the control. Resource lookups see the objects being read. Section references are bounded: depth, offsets, counts, unknown kinds fail the load. Layout per the public description of the format in XbfAnalyzer (Apache-2.0); the reader is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
